{"questions":[{"question_id":"NlQwrJQxyidRbufT","paperTitle":"AIEEE 2011","year":2011,"examDate":2011,"subject":"chemistry","chapter":"chemical-bonding-and-molecular-structure","chapterGroup":"inorganic-chemistry","topic":"ionic-bond","type":"mcq","marks":4,"negMarks":1,"permalink":"among-the-following-the-maximum-covalent-character-is-shown-2011-marks-4-nlqwrjqxyidrbuft.htm","content":"Among the following the maximum covalent character is shown by the compound : ","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"SnCl<sub>2 </sub>"},{"identifier":"B","content":"AlCl<sub>3</sub> "},{"identifier":"C","content":"MgCl<sub>2 </sub>"},{"identifier":"D","content":"FeCl<sub>2</sub>"}],"correct_options":["B"],"explanation":"Charge of cation/Size of cation is called polarising power.\n<br><br><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.186ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.509ex\" height=\"1.251ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -471 667 553\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2234\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2234\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> (i) Polarising power <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.76ex\" height=\"1.025ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -442 778 453\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"221D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-221D\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> charge of cation\n<br><br>(ii) Polarising power <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.76ex\" height=\"1.025ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -442 778 453\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"221D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-221D\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> <span style=\"display: inline-block;vertical-align: middle;\">\n     <div style=\"text-align: center;border-bottom: 1px solid black;\">1</div>\n     <div style=\"text-align: center;\">size of cation</div>\n</span>\n<br><br>Here the AlCl<sub>3</sub>\n is satisfying the above two conditions i.e., Al\nis in +3 oxidation state and also has small size. So it has more\ncovalent character.\n"}]}